It reads the data of the Victron Energy installations of the user through the
official VRM API v2 (https://vrm-api-docs.victronenergy.com), with a personal
access token of the user's own VRM account. This integration is not
affiliated with nor endorsed by Victron Energy. The endpoints, fields and
limits follow the official documentation and answers of the live API; its
scope was compared with the Home Assistant "Victron Remote Monitoring"
integration and its "victron-vrm" library (https://github.com/KSoft-Si/vrm-client,
MIT License). No code is taken from either.
